<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Lancaster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1399–1471</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Lancaster was a branch of the English royal house of Plantagenet, descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-gaunt">John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster</a>. It held the throne from 1399, when Henry IV deposed Richard II, through Henry V, victor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-agincourt">Agincourt</a>, to Henry VI. Its rivalry with the House of York led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>, and its line ended with Henry VI's death in 1471.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-lancaster.jpg" alt="House of Lancaster" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Edmund_Crouchback,_Earl_of_Leicester_and_Lancaster.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
